system role

The system role is a special instruction that sets the permanent rules, personality, and boundaries for the AI model before the user ever types a single word.
Think of it as programming the AI's attitude and behavior.
While your code runs inside the loop, the user role changes with every new prompt you type, but the system role stays completely locked in to control how the AI reacts to you.

🎭 The 3 Core Roles Explained
To see why the system role is so unique, look at how it compares to the other roles you send to the SDK:

system	- The Director / Boss	Sets the background rules, tone, constraints, and persona (e.g., "You are a strict math teacher").
user	  - You (The Human)	Sends the actual dynamic questions, code snippets, or tasks into the terminal loop.
assistant -	The AI Model	The output response generated back to you by the model based on the system instructions.


