temperature

Think of Temperature as a knob that controls how creative or how strict the AI is.
Imagine the AI is an assistant you are talking to:
• Low Temperature (0.0): The AI acts like a strict scientist. It will only tell you direct, proven facts. If you ask it the same question 10 times, it will give you the exact same answer every single time. It never takes risks.
• High Temperature (1.0 or higher): The AI acts like an artist or storyteller. It gets highly creative, uses wild imagination, and tells stories. If you ask it the exact same question twice, it will give you completely different, unique answers.

Why do we use it in code?
When you are building your chatbot, you pass this number to the SDK:
• If you want the AI to write perfect Python code, you set temperature=0.0 (because you want strict rules, not artistic code).
• If you want the AI to write a poem or a movie script, you set temperature=1.0 (because you want it to be creative).

